G2610.b:
*† ⟪κατ-αγωνίζομαι⟫, depon., "perfective" compound (M, Pr., 116);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to struggle against⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to conquer⟫, ⟪overcome⟫: ⟦Hebrews 11:33|He 11:33⟧.†

G2614.b:
⟪κατα-διώκω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨רדף⁩;] "perfective" compound (M, Pr., 116), ⟪to pursue closely⟫, ⟪follow up⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ with hostile intent (Thuc., i, 49, ⟦Genesis 31:36|Ge 31:36⟧ al.);
⟪(b)⟫ with kindly intention (⟦Psalms 23:6|Ps 22 (23):6⟧, ⟦1 Samuel 30:22|I Ki 30:22⟧, cf. Si 27:17): ⟦Mark 1:36|Mk 1:36⟧.†

G2634.b:
⟪κατα-κυριεύω⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Genesis 1:28|Ge 1:28⟧ (⁨כּבשׁ⁩), ⟦Psalms 110:2|Ps 109 (110):2⟧ (⁨רדה⁩) Si 17:4, al.;] ⟪to gain⟫ or ⟪exercise dominion (over)⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ absol. (Arist.);
⟪(b)⟫ c. gen. (Arist., al.): ⟦Matthew 20:25|Mt 20:25⟧, ⟦Mark 10:42|Mk 10:42⟧, ⟦Acts 19:16|Ac 19:16⟧, ⟦1 Peter 5:3|I Pe 5:3⟧.†
SYN.: (κατεξουσιάζω) (v. Swete, Mk., l.c.).

G2675.b:
⟪κατ-αρτίζω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly in Pss (⟦Psalms 8:2|8:2⟧ al.; ⁨כּוּן⁩, etc.) and II Es (⁨כְּלַל⁩);] ⟪to render⟫ ἄρτιος, i.e. ⟪fit⟫, ⟪complete⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to mend⟫, ⟪repair⟫: ⟦Matthew 4:21|Mt 4:21⟧, ⟦Mark 1:19|Mk 1:19⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to furnish completely⟫, ⟪complete⟫, ⟪equip⟫, ⟪prepare⟫: pass., ⟦Luke 6:40|Lk 6:40⟧, ⟦Romans 9:22|Ro 9:22⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:3|He 11:3⟧; mid., ⟦Matthew 21:16|Mt 21:16⟧(LXX), ⟦Hebrews 10:5|He 10:5⟧(LXX);
⟪(c)⟫ in ethical sense, ⟪to prepare⟫, ⟪complete⟫, ⟪perfect⟫: ⟦Galatians 6:1|Ga 6:1⟧ (EV, restore), ⟦1 Peter 5:10|I Pe 5:10⟧; pass., ⟦1 Corinthians 1:10|I Co 1:10⟧ (Field, Notes, 167), ⟦2 Corinthians 13:11|II Co 13:11⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:21|He 13:21⟧ (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
